-- title:
--   Non-vanishing of the near-branch node value at supersingular nodes
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$, and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ whose kernel is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$ (hypothesis `hker`). Let $a \in k$ lie in `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$; assume $a^{q^2} = a$, $a \neq 0$ and $a \neq 1728$. Let $f$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series. Assume the Laurent series of $f$ and of its Fricke transform `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q) f` both lie in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, and that the images of both under `CharPReduction.modularRedLocHom` lie in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` (the subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`) and are nonzero. Assume further (`hford`) that for every place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ one has $W.\mathrm{ord}\, f = 0$ as soon as $W$ is centred at the node, in the sense that there are $x, y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\, x = a$, $\mathrm{red}\, y = a^q$, $W.\mathrm{ord}(j_q - x) > 0$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j_q(q\tau) - y) > 0$, where $j_q$ and its $q$-expansion rescaling `qExpand ℚ (1 * q) jq` are viewed in the field via `coeffEmb`. Finally let $c \in k$ and suppose the first place of `frobNodePair q a`, namely `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a`, takes the value $c$ at the reduction of $f$, i.e. that reduction lies in the corresponding valuation subring and its residue is the image of $c$. Then $c \neq 0$.
--
--   This is a step in the local study of the tube around a supersingular node of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(q)$ in characteristic $q$: a function with no zero or pole at any place centred at the node $(a, a^q)$ cannot reduce to a function vanishing at the node on the branch through the cusp. It is used in [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_twoBranchNormalisation_qpow_and_ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_eq_neg`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.exists_twoBranchNormalisation_qpow_and_ord_charLGeomPlaceOfPoint_eq_neg) and in [`ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.isUnit_evalAt_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero_of_gaussUnit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.NodeLocalized.isUnit_evalAt_of_forall_centred_ord_eq_zero_of_gaussUnit).
